    "created_at": "2023-03-08T18:44:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-08T18:46:25Z",
    "body": "@domenic I would be glad to have CSS configured to prefer its own terms internally somehow if that's possible; @tabatkins is that possible? (Splitting into modules is useful to us in a lot of ways but it definitely makes cross-linking more of a mess.)\r\n\r\nThat said, I do think the DOM spec would be easier to read if the “start” and “end” concepts were a bit more specific, regardless, though, so maybe we can do both? At least I found things easier to read when reviewing the built results of the patch here, and I suspect Tab's follow-up suggestion of using “start point” and “end point” would have a similar effect. The extra word helps anchor it as a technical term referring to a particular data member, rather than as its more general English usage.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
